rature readings would fail.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.2\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The most likely anomaly is the PCA9685 A0 address pin tied to +3.3V rather than GND, which shifts the PWM driver's I2C address from the specified 0x40 to 0x41. A lower-confidence address mismatch also appears on the TMP100 sensor.\"\n}",
